Finding the cycle start in `0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 2` (node 4 points back to node 2):

| move | slow | fast |
|---|---|---|
| start | 0 | 0 |
| 1 | 1 | 2 |
| 2 | 2 | 4 |
| 3 | 3 | 3 ← they meet |

Restart slow at 0; move both one step: slow 1, fast 4; slow 2, fast 2 — **node 2** is the start of the cycle.

Removing the k-th node from the end, with a dummy node so the head is no special case:

```cpp
Node dummy(0, head);
Node* lead = &dummy;
Node* trail = &dummy;
for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) lead = lead->next;
while (lead->next) { lead = lead->next; trail = trail->next; }
trail->next = trail->next->next;   // unlink the target
head = dummy.next;
```

